 "dx9_only": [],
 "notes": "Group H = 97 SE methods with 'cam' in the method name on non-camera classes. sMediator camera accessors are all inlined in DX9: mpCamera at +0xD0 (SE +0x140), mpCameraBoss at +0xD4 (SE +0x144); setMiniGameCameraInfo is SE-only. MP: mpCamera is one singleton camera slot and must become per-player; every reader (enemy/player vibration requests, uDevil4Model camera transparency, cEventScript::killBossCamera, uEm008_009Base::getCameraPositionLR, uEm025::resetCamera, cPopeCommon::setCameraVib, uHugeStatue::setCameraVibration) assumes one camera. H methods that also read per-player state: uEm022::setBusterCameraEnd (mpPlayer->mPlayerID==1), cEventScript::killBossCamera (mpPlayer gate), uDevil4Model::getCameraTransparency AABB/Sphere (getPlayerPos in SE). DX9 sVibration: the existing placeholder names sVibration::req_simple/req_at_pos/req_with_parent/alloc_slot/rec_* (commented as 'particle_pool') are really SE sVibration::reqVib overloads / openVibControl / VibControl::start / updateFadeParam (0x90A1B0 = 4th callee of VibControl::move 0x909CA0, like SE updateFadeParam 1031 B). Not renamed by H; the coordinator should reconcile. The DX9 caller of killBossCamera is named 'sGameState::player_spawn_state' (0x44A910) but corresponds to SE cEventScript::executeCode. ICF folds: uEm022::setBusterCameraStart == uEm023::reqBusterCamera (0x6B56E0); uEm016::reqCamVib == uEm031::reqCamVib == uEmAngelo::setCameraVib (0x618360); uEm019::camera_vib_ctrl == uEm019_00::camera_vib_ctrl (0x64D540); uEm019::setBossCameraStatus == uEm021::setBossCameraStatus (0x65B540); uPlayerDanteBoss::setCameraVib == uPlayer::setCameraVibration (0x7C62E0); uGetItem::getCamera is a generic getter (0x744100). uDevil4Model overload suffixes: _3 = MtAABB, _2 = MtSphere, base = void (names kept)."
